      "text": "pursuant to the New York City Loan Guarantee Act of 1978, P. L. 95-339, as the same\nmay be from time to time amended, an Agreement to Guarantee by and among the United\nStates of America, the State of New York, The City of New York, the New York State\nFinancial Control Board and the Municipal Assistance Corporation for The City of New\nYork, a Loan Agreement between The City of New York and certain banks and pension\nfunds, and a Guaranteed Bond Purchase Agreement by and among The City of New York,\ncertain City pension funds, certain State pension funds and the United States of America,\neach dated as of November 15, 1978, including, but not limited to, full power to execute for,\non behalf of, and at the direction of the Mayor, any document pursuant to any such agreement\nand any agreement, amendment to agreement or other document pursuant to such law. The\nexercise of functions, powers and duties for, on behalf of and at the direction of the Mayor\nby such Deputy Mayor pursuant to this delegation shall not require the consent in writing of\nthe Mayor or any other official of the City.",
